---
import CodeTabs from '../../components/CodeTabs.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Rate limiting">
  <p>
    The API uses <strong>two-tier rate limiting</strong>. When you go over the normal limit,
    cached responses still come through, up to a second, higher limit.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <div class="tier-diagram">
    <div class="tier">
      <div class="tier-header">
        <span class="tier-badge normal">Tier 1: Normal</span>
      </div>
      <p>Standard rate limit for all requests. Can fetch fresh lyrics or serve from cache.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-arrow">When exceeded</div>
    <div class="tier">
      <div class="tier-header">
        <span class="tier-badge cached">Tier 2: Cached</span>
      </div>
      <p>Higher rate limit, but only serves cached responses. Fresh fetches return 429.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-arrow">When exceeded</div>
    <div class="tier">
      <div class="tier-header">
        <span class="tier-badge exceeded">Rate limited</span>
      </div>
      <p>All requests return 429 Too Many Requests.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>
    Limits are per IP address. The limits can change, so do not hardcode them.
    Read <code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code> and <code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code> on each response instead.
  </p>

  <h2>Response headers</h2>
  <p>The API reports rate limit, cache and authentication state in these headers:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Header</th>
        <th>Values</th>
        <th>When it is sent</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code></td>
        <td>Burst size of the current tier. On <code>exceeded</code> it is the burst size of the cached tier.</td>
        <td>Every request without a valid API key</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code></td>
        <td>Requests left in the current tier, <code>0</code> when both tiers are exceeded</td>
        <td>Every request without a valid API key</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-RateLimit-Type</code></td>
        <td><code>normal</code>, <code>cached</code>, <code>exceeded</code>, or <code>bypass</code></td>
        <td>Every request without a valid API key. With a valid API key, <code>bypass</code> is sent on JSON responses from the lyrics endpoints, <code>/revalidate</code> and the <code>/cache/*</code> endpoints</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-RateLimit-Bypass</code></td>
        <td><code>true</code></td>
        <td>Requests with a valid <code>X-API-Key</code> header</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Retry-After</code></td>
        <td><code>1</code> when both tiers are exceeded, <code>60</code> when the cached tier has no cache entry for the query</td>
        <td>Only on <code>429</code> responses</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-Cache-Status</code></td>
        <td><code>HIT</code>, <code>MISS</code>, <code>NEGATIVE_HIT</code>, or <code>STALE</code> (<code>STALE</code> only on <code>/getLyrics</code>)</td>
        <td>Lyrics endpoints: <code>/getLyrics</code> and the provider-specific endpoints. See <a href="/docs/caching">Caching</a></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-Provider</code></td>
        <td><code>ttml</code>, <code>kugou</code>, or <code>qq</code></td>
        <td>Provider-specific endpoints only, for example <code>/kugou/getLyrics</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>X-Auth-Mode</code></td>
        <td><code>authenticated</code>, <code>invalid</code>, or <code>cache</code></td>
        <td><code>/getLyrics</code>, <code>/ttml/getLyrics</code> and <code>/revalidate</code>, when the API requires a key for uncached queries. See <a href="/docs/authentication">Authentication</a></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="callout" role="note">
    <div class="callout-body">
      <p>
        Browsers cannot read these headers from cross-origin JavaScript. The API does not expose them
        through CORS on purpose, so they are meant for server-side callers and tools like curl.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Rate limit types</h2>

  <h3><code>normal</code></h3>
  <p>Request processed normally. Can fetch fresh lyrics or serve from cache.</p>

  <h3><code>cached</code></h3>
  <p>
    Normal tier exceeded. The request is served only if the lyrics are cached.
    Otherwise it returns 429.
  </p>

  <h3><code>exceeded</code></h3>
  <p>Both tiers exceeded. All requests return 429 Too Many Requests.</p>

  <h3><code>bypass</code></h3>
  <p>The request has a valid API key, so rate limits do not apply.</p>

  <h2>API key bypass</h2>
  <p>
    Requests with a valid <code>X-API-Key</code> header bypass all rate limits.
    This is useful for production applications that need guaranteed access.
  </p>
  <CodeTabs tabs={[
    { language: 'curl', code: `curl -H "X-API-Key: your-api-key" \\
  "https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154"` },
    { language: 'javascript', code: `const res = await fetch("https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154", {
  headers: { "X-API-Key": "your-api-key" },
});
const data = await res.json();` },
    { language: 'python', code: `import requests

res = requests.get(
    "https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154",
    headers={"X-API-Key": "your-api-key"},
)
data = res.json()` },
    { language: 'go', code: `package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"io"
	"net/http"
)

func main() {
	req, err := http.NewRequest(http.MethodGet, "https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154", nil)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	req.Header.Set("X-API-Key", "your-api-key")

	res, err := http.DefaultClient.Do(req)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	defer res.Body.Close()

	body, err := io.ReadAll(res.Body)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	fmt.Println(string(body))
}` },
  ]} />
  <p>
    When bypass is active, every response includes <code>X-RateLimit-Bypass: true</code>, and has no
    <code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code> or <code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code>. The lyrics endpoints,
    <code>/revalidate</code> and the <code>/cache/*</code> JSON responses also include <code>X-RateLimit-Type: bypass</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-bash">X-RateLimit-Bypass: true
X-RateLimit-Type: bypass</code></pre>

  <h2>Handling rate limits</h2>
  <p>When you receive a 429 response:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Check the <code>Retry-After</code> header for when to retry</li>
    <li>Check <code>X-RateLimit-Type</code> to see which tier was exceeded</li>
    <li>If <code>cached</code>, the lyrics are not in the cache yet, so wait before you retry</li>
    <li>Use exponential backoff for retries</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Rate limit responses</h2>
  <p>
    When both tiers are exhausted, any endpoint returns <code>429 Too Many Requests</code> with
    <code>Content-Type: text/plain</code>, <code>Retry-After: 1</code> and <code>X-RateLimit-Type: exceeded</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code>Too Many Requests</code></pre>
  <p>
    When the cached tier serves a lyrics request that is not cached, the response is <code>429</code> with a JSON body,
    <code>Retry-After: 60</code> and <code>X-RateLimit-Type: cached</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "Rate limit exceeded. This request requires cached data, but no cache is available for this query.",
  "message": "Please try again later or reduce your request rate."
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The provider-specific endpoints return <code>{`{"error": "Rate limit exceeded. No cached data available.", "provider": "..."}`}</code> in this case.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .tier-diagram {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  .tier {
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-4);
  }

  .tier-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .tier-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .tier-badge.normal {
    background-color: rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.1);
    color: var(--success);
  }

  .tier-badge.cached {
    background-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.1);
    color: var(--warning);
  }

  .tier-badge.exceeded {
    background-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.1);
    color: var(--error);
  }

  .tier p {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .tier ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .tier-arrow {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    padding: var(--space-1) 0;
  }
</style>
